Copy and punctuate these direct speech sentences.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Rose said We are your new neighbours.
\item We should make them feel welcome said Father Mouse.
\item Shall we invite them for tea asked Mother Mouse.
\end{enumerate}

All the letters of these words are jumbled up. Rearrange the letters so that they make meaningful words.
\begin{enumerate}
\item neniusatal
\item stwgeee
\item eensegmnt
\item ceshrt
\item nburi
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Hints}

\begin{enumerate}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{a}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{connect}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{g}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{been}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{s}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{segment}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{r}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{right}
\item The answer starts with the letter \emph{b}\\
The meaning of this word (in English) :\\
\emph{brown}
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item aansluiten
\item geweest
\item segmenten
\item rechts
\item bruin
\end{enumerate}

Calculate the difference between 963 and 389.

\subsection*{Answers}
The difference is 574.

Calculate \( 837 \div 9 \).

\subsection*{Answers}
The answer is 93.

Write the plural of the following nouns:  
\begin{enumerate}
    \item Actriz
    \item Pantalones
    \item Camión
    \item Pez
    \item Jueves
\end{enumerate}

\subsection*{Answers}
\begin{enumerate}
\item Actrices
\item Pantalones
\item Camiones
\item Peces
\item Jueves
\end{enumerate}
